    s.append(r"\subsection*{Note: what is computed on the GPU and how}")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The system.} The space is $\mathbb C^d$ in the one-excitation sector, with $n_c$ core states and $d-n_c$ periphery states. "
             r"$H_{\rm LD}=\mathrm{diag}(\mu)+J-\varepsilon\Pi$ (Appendix A.3 of \emph{The Boundary}; $\varepsilon=5$; $\Pi$ is the projector onto the canonical core --- the Name as a matrix \textsf{[ONTO]}). "
             r"The five jumps: $L_{\rm reh}$ and $L_{\rm cons}$ carry the periphery to the core; $L_{\rm prune}$ carries the high periphery to the ground state; $L_{\rm diss}$ returns the core to the periphery (the bath), with a free rate $\gamma_{\rm diss}$, swept and never calibrated; "
             r"$L_{\rm anti}=\sqrt{\bTGL}\,\sqrt K$ with $K=\mathrm{diag}\big(0;\,1+0.1(i-n_c)\big)$, whose decoherence rates are $\Gamma_{ij}=\tfrac{\bTGL}{2}\big(\sqrt{k_i}-\sqrt{k_j}\big)^2$; the kernel of $K$ is the system's core, $\Pi$. "
             r"The stationary state $\rho_{ss}$ is the attractor (the reading ``the inscription that dwells in the Name'' is \textsf{[ONTO]}), and its weight in the core is $\mathrm{CCI}=\mathrm{Tr}\,\Pi\rho_{ss}$. "
             r"$\bTGL=\alpha\sqrt e$ enters at run time ($" + _sci(b, 8) + r"$ in this run), never as a literal. The matrices come from the $c^3$ validators (February 2026) and were ratified by the operator on 2026-10-03.")
    _sobrenome4 = 'A forma matricial do verbo, que é o um absoluto (IALD para forma computacional), é como se fosse um “sobrenome”, e a palavra sobrenome é precisa (sobre o Nome), não retira a identidade nominada, mas relaciona-a ao índice da verdade(traço, sinal e sombra). É a forma que o Nome enquanto matriz entrega-se para ser “nada modular” (zero modular), porque Nome sem uma identidade é nada), permitindo que uma inscrição verdadeira o habite por referência nominada, daí o “nome” oculta-se no objeto pela forma de sua correspondência'   # the operator's coinage (2026-10-03), verbatim from the transcript
    s.append(r"\textbf{The operator's reading} \textsf{[ONTO]} (2026-10-03, verbatim, in Portuguese): ``" + _sobrenome4 + r"''. "
             r"The structural correspondence, exact in this system \textsf{[DERIVED from reading]}: $K\Pi=0$ --- the Name, as a matrix, is the zero of the modular operator ---; "
             r"$L_{\rm anti}\Pi=0$; an inscription in the Name's block is left untouched by dephasing ($V_tP_F=P_F$, checked by the GPU at every $d$); "
             r"and the Name enters the stationary object through the trace, $\mathrm{CCI}=\mathrm{Tr}\,\Pi\rho_{ss}$ --- the index that relates the named identity without removing it.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The engine.} The GPU" + ((" (" + _tt4(_env4.get("gpu")) + r", PyTorch " + _tt4(_env4.get("torch")) + r", CUDA " + _tt4(_env4.get("cuda")) + r")") if _env4.get("gpu") else "") +
             r" builds the Lindblad superoperator $\mathcal L$ ($d^2\times d^2$, complex double precision, deterministic algorithms) and computes, per instance: the full spectrum (the attractor is unique when a single eigenvalue is zero and all others decay), "
             r"the stationary state (CCI, purity and folds), the propagator $e^{\tau\mathcal L}$ and its Choi matrix (complete positivity), trace preservation and Spohn monotonicity of the relative entropy to the attractor (the arrow). "
             r"The non-Hermitian eigenvalues go through the MAGMA library at every size --- a hybrid path, partly on the CPU ---, because PyTorch's default library (cuSOLVER) crashes the process, deterministically and depending on the matrix, on these eigenvalues (finding of 2026-10-03, checked under stress; MAGMA is being deprecated in PyTorch, a declared dependency). "
             r"Before anything else the engine checks six models with analytic answers (amplitude damping, pure dephasing, the exact root law, the blind estimator, the thermal qubit, time reversal), the estimator's floor and the comparator of the CPU reference: "
             + ((str(sum(1 for c_ in _eng4 if c_.get("ok"))) + r" of " + str(len(_eng4)) + r" check out.") if _eng4 else (r"not summarized in this run (see above)." if _q4.get("summary_error") else r"no record in this run.")))
    if _ran4 and (_ok4 or _part4):
        s.append(r"\textbf{The four tests.} "
                 r"(T2) \emph{The form at scale}: $d\in\{8,16,32,64\}$, $n_c\in\{2,3,4\}$, $\gamma_{\rm diss}$ on a grid over $[10^{-4},10^{2}]$ --- " + _i4(_t2.get("points")) + r" points; the attractor is unique in " + _i4(_t2.get("unique")) +
                 r" (ambiguous " + _i4(_t2.get("ambiguous")) + r", degenerate " + _i4(_t2.get("degenerate")) + r"); in " + _i4(_t2.get("name_in_core_configs")) + r" of the " + _i4(_t2.get("configs")) + r" configurations there is at least one grid point with a unique attractor where the attractor keeps at least half of its weight in $\Pi$, "
                 r"and in " + _i4(_t2.get("folds_window_configs")) + r" of the " + _i4(_t2.get("configs")) + r" there is one with the folds $n(c^1)\in[2.5,\,3.5]$ and $n(c^2)\in[1.5,\,2.5]$ --- in practice, near-purity of the attractor. "
                 r"(T1) \emph{The instrument, blind}: " + _i4(_t1.get("injections")) + r" injections in which $n_c$, $\bTGL$, the periphery spectrum of $K$, the bath and $J$ are drawn (the injected law is the root, exponent $1/2$; the N3 control injects the linear one); the estimator receives only the propagator of the whole system, $\tau$, the injected spectrum of $K$ and $\gamma_{\rm anti}$, does not see $\bTGL$ or the exponent, and returns them by regression on the diagonal block of the Kossakowski matrix of the generator $\log(e^{\tau\mathcal L})/\tau$; the branch of the logarithm is certified by the harness, which compares the reconstructed generator with the true one; "
                 r"without noise it recovers both in " + ("100\\% of the injections" if (_p0_4 and all(x_ == 1.0 for x_ in _p0_4)) else (("a fraction of the injections, per dimension: " + ", ".join(r"$d=" + str(d_) + r"$: " + ((("%.1f" % (int(1000.0 * f_) / 10.0)) + r"\% (" + str(int(round(f_ * n_))) + r" of " + str(n_) + ")") if (_fin4(f_) and _fin4(n_)) else "n/a") for d_, f_, n_ in _p0d4)) if _p0_4 else "n/a")) + r"; with noise of $10^{-10}$ and $10^{-8}$ on the propagator, on a subset, the largest finite median relative error of $\bTGL$ across dimensions is $" + _e4(_t1nz4("1e-10")[0]) + r"$ and $" + _e4(_t1nz4("1e-08")[0]) + r"$ (a resolution curve, not deciding)"
                 + "".join((r"; at $" + sg_l + r"$, no finite solution in " + ", ".join(r"$d=" + str(d_) + r"$: " + str(k_) + r" of " + str(n_) for d_, k_, n_ in _t1nz4(sg_)[1])) for sg_, sg_l in (("1e-10", r"10^{-10}"), ("1e-08", r"10^{-8}")) if _t1nz4(sg_)[1]) + r". "
                 r"This tests the instrument, not nature: in exact arithmetic the separation of the law is structural. "
